      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Magnetic resonance imaging is a useful tool for investigating causes of abdominal pain in pregnancy. Differentiating between physiologic hydronephrosis of pregnancy and pathologic hydronephrosis can be challenging for clinicians and radiologists. This report describes loss of the India ink artifact around the obstructed kidney as a novel and potentially useful radiological sign, which may be of value in the evaluation of abdominal pain and hydronephrosis in pregnancy."
      },
